<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ Real Wage Rate Index falls 0.6 pct in June qtr.</title>
<headline>NZ Real Wage Rate Index falls 0.6 pct in June qtr.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The purchasing power of New Zealand wages and salaries fell in the June 1996 quarter when compared to the March 1996 quarter, Statistics New Zealand said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;A 0.2 percent rise in the After-tax Wage Rate Index was offset by a 0.8 percent increase in the Consumers' Price Index (CPI) resulting in a 0.6 percent decrease in the Real Wage Rate Index over the quarter,&quot; SNZ said.  </p>
<p>Over the year to June 1996, the Real Wage Rate Index (RWRI) dropped by 0.3 percent. SNZ said the annual decrease resulted from consumer prices (up 2.0 percent) rising faster than after-tax wages and salaries (up to 1.7 percent).</p>
</text>
